  "rhythm": "Songsterr s43738, the original Mega Drive arrangement (slap bass, two synth brasses, square and saw leads, strings, glockenspiel, electric piano, pad, drums) at its 150 BPM. The ocarina plays the main theme from Track 1 (synth brass), bars 9-16 note for note: the pickup on bar 9 beat 3, the tune twice with its answers, ending on the low C held to the bar line; rests kept. Shortest note an eighth (0.2 s), full speed, 12.8 s. The 4-bar intro (bars 0-3) is the band's count-in (intro_beats 16, the most the drum engine takes), so the ocarina line opens with a 2-beat rest (bar 9's first two beats) before the pickup; bars 4-8 (the groove before the tune) are skipped. Band, all from the tab: its drums (kick, snare, hats) for bars 0-3 and 9-16, with soft sixteenth hats added under the intro's arpeggios so every onset sits on a hit; its slap bass an octave up (A2..B3); parts: the synth brass (Track 1's rising intro arpeggios and Track 2's intro chords, then Track 2's falling counter-line under the tune), the glockenspiel doubling the tune an octave above the ocarina (soft), and the square lead's falling C-B-A-G twinkle in the intro. Same key as the record (the ocarina an octave down). General MIDI sound font (synth brass, glockenspiel, square lead). || 2026-09-30 extension for jelster64: the theme's last bar is now its second-time ending (bar 24: the held low C becomes the C-C-E pickup) and the bridge's first phrase follows (bars 25-27, track 1: D held, C-D into a long E, rests kept), 12 new beats ending where that phrase ends; the second bridge phrase would pass the 16-beat extension. Bars 17-23 repeat 9-15 note for note, so they were skipped. Band over the new bars from the same tracks: drums, slap bass, synth brass, the glockenspiel doubling, and the square lead's falling bridge counter-melody (A#-A-G, F-E-D, A-B-C) above the ocarina. 44 beats = 17.6 s after the 6.4 s intro, full tempo. || 2026-09-30 second extension for sonickrazy (asked for all the way to the high notes ",
